          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Tate K-theory is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology+theory"} elliptic cohomology theory
            associated with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+curve"} Tate curve
            (the Tate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+series"} Laurent series
            ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}((q))
            ) (
            %a{:href => "#AHS01"}> AHS 01, 2.7
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 09, 4.3
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (
            %a{:href => "#AHS01"}> AHS 01, Sec. 2.7
            ).
          %h3#plain_version Plain version
          %p
            The underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} cohomology theory
            is given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+series"} Laurent series
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+spaces"} free loop spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}(-)
            (
            %a{:href => "#KM04"}> KM 04, Section 5
            , see also
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 09, Section 5.2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Ell
                            %mi Tate
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi K
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Ell_{Tate}(X)
                  \&amp;
                  \\simeq
                  \\;
                  K(X)((q))
                  \\\
                  \&amp;
                  \\simeq
                  \\;
                  K_{S^1}(\mathcal{L}X)
                  \\otimes_{K_{S^1}(\ast)}
                  \\mathbb{Z}((q))
                  \\,.
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            (For more exposition see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Dove19"} Dove 19, Sec. 6.2
          %h3#IdeaEquivariantVersion Equivariant version
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            version of Tate K-theory is a form of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
            it comes down (
            %a{:href => "#Ganter07"}> Ganter 07, Def. 3.1
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ganter13"} Ganter 13, Def. 2.6
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Dove19"} Dove 19, Def. 6.16
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ell
                    %mi Tate
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo ≺
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
