                  \\Lambda_g \;\coloneqq\; \frac{C_g \times \mathbb{R}}{ \langle (g^{-1},1) \rangle }
          %p
            appearing
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Huan's+inertia+orbifold#HuanCentralizer"} there
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
            with that of a rotation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
          %p
            Hence, in generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+ad-equivariant+K-theory"} twisted ad-equivariant K-theory
            there is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+ad-equivariant+Tate+K-theory"} twisted ad-equivariant Tate K-theory
            (an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            theory) relating to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"} Verlinde ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+representation"} positive energy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group+representations"} loop group representations
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie 09, Sec. 5.2
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Luecke19"} Luecke 19, Cor. 3.2.5
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Dove19"} Dove 19
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_elliptic_genus Relation to elliptic genus
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ochanine+genus"} Ochanine genus
            lifts to a homomorphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo →
                  %mi KO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M Spin \to KO((q))
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+K-theory"} Tate K-theory
            (
            %a{:href => "spin-orientation+of+elliptic+cohomology#KreckStolz93"}> Kreck-Stolz 93, lemma 5.8, lemma 5.4
            ). This is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-orientation+of+elliptic+cohomology"} spin-orientation of elliptic cohomology
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
